{
  "version": 1,
  "name": "Example: Switches and a breaker",
  "exampleId": "block-switches",
  "description": "Each circuit is 10 V into a 10 Ω load, 1 A when closed. The ideal switch follows a 5 Hz pulse on its gate. The closing switch closes at 0.1 s and the opening switch opens then. The two-way switch moves the current from a 10 Ω load (1 A) to a 20 Ω load (0.5 A). The breaker opens a 10 Ω, 10 mH circuit at 0.1 s: its arc voltage rises from 30 V until it forces the current to zero.",
  "duration": 0.3,
  "revision": 0,
